OL,3,GNEWSAUS and Ireland's relationship
OL,4,A'stronger than ever'
OL,5,
OL,6,FUS President Donald Trump has said his
OL,7,Fcountry's relationship with Ireland is
OL,8,F"stronger than ever".
OL,10,FHe's on a two-day visit to the country
OL,11,Fwhere he is meeting with Taoiseach
OL,12,F(Irish Prime Minister) Micheal Martin
OL,13,Fat Farmleigh House, in Phoenix Park.
OL,15,FTrump's first visit was to the Aras an
OL,16,FUachtarain - the official residence of
OL,17,Fthe Irish president - where he had a
OL,18,Fcourtesy call with Irish President
OL,19,FCatherine Connolly.
OL,23,APub: 11-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
